research/private/

# local scratch
scratch/

# Gazette originals and everything derived from them.
#
# These directories hold a board's original PDFs and 138,617 named students'
# results. Nothing in either may ever reach the repository.
#
# WHOLE DIRECTORIES, ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH. Two versions of this rule
# were wrong before this one:
#
#   gazette/*.pdf   left a hole — any other file dropped in there (an extracted
#                   .jsonl, a debug dump, a sample page) would be committed.
#   gazette/        closed that hole and opened a worse one: a pattern with no
#                   leading slash matches at EVERY level, so it silently
#                   excluded scripts/gazette/ — the parser itself — from the
#                   commit. Caught because the staged file list came up short.
/gazette/
/gazette-private/
__pycache__/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal

# os / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
